Name: Simple Homomorphic Encryption Library with Lattices
URL: https://github.com/google/shell-encryption
Version: f94f58852e9b3edaf2766e348a69a70f596bb9dd
Revision: f94f58852e9b3edaf2766e348a69a70f596bb9dd
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: Apache-2.0
License File: src/LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description: This project is a library for fully-homomorphic symmetric-key
encryption. It uses Ring Learning with Errors (RLWE)-based encryption to make it
possible to both add and multiply encrypted data. It uses modulus-switching to
enable arbitrary-depth homomorphic encryption (provided sufficiently large
parameters are set). RLWE is also believed to be secure in the face of quantum
computers.

Local Modifications:
patches/0001-lite-runtime-protos.patch: Build the protos with
  LITE_RUNTIME, as Chromium links protobuf_lite, and compare them by
  serialized bytes.
patches/0002-fls64-no-dcheck.patch: Comment out the DCHECK_NE in
  Fls64().
patches/0003-Support-SHELL-tests-in-chromium.patch: Build the tests in
  Chromium.
patches/0004-Support-SHELL-component-build.patch: Export the public
  classes for the component build.
patches/0005-Add-SHELL-go-package.patch: Set go_package in
  serialization.proto.
patches/0006-Quit-using-ValueOrDie.patch: Make rlwe::StatusOr an alias
  of absl::StatusOr.
patches/0007-Fix-Wunused-function-Wunused-local-typedef.patch: Fix
  -Wunused-function and -Wunused-local-typedef.
patches/0008-Fix-Wsign-compare.patch: Fix -Wsign-compare and
  -Wignored-qualifiers.
patches/0009-Drop-std-has_denorm-_loss-deprecated-in-C-23.patch: Drop
  std::has_denorm, deprecated in C++23.
patches/0010-use-std-optional.patch: Use std::optional instead of
  absl::optional.

Update instructions:
Update commit hashes in crowbar.txtpb, then run from this directory:
crowbar build --no-dry-run ./
copy.bara.sky lists every file it imports. If the new upstream version
adds a file Chromium needs, add it there and to BUILD.gn.
